<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Celje</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Celeia, Cilli</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Celje is the third-largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a>, on the Savinja River. As Celeia it was a Celtic settlement and then a Roman town of Noricum, granted municipal status under Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a>. In the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the seat of the powerful Counts of Cilli, whose line died out in 1456. It later formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/celje.jpg" alt="Celje" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Reisevogel · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Celjski_dom_in_Celje.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
